  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Shelter and Non-food Item (NFI) Assistance to Flood-Affected People in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since March 2024, the long rains season fueled by erratic El-Ni&#xF1;o patterns, including heavy storms and flash floods affected various parts of Kenya and is expected to continue throughout May 2024. Several counties have been affected by floods, resulting in loss of lives, properties, and disruption of services including cutting off main roads. Over 412,000 people have been affected and more than 290,000 people displaced across the country. The floods have increased the risk of food security, malnutrition, water-borne diseases and protection issues. With the requested support from the Central Emergency Response Fund&#x2019;s Rapid Response Window, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is scaling up the response to address the most pressing needs of the flood-affected population, prioritizing the most vulnerable populations, targeting Garissa, Kilifi, Homa Bay, Tana River and Nairobi counties. The project contributes to meeting the basic needs of the flood-affected population in Kenya by supporting them to have minimum living conditions through shelter and non-food item (NFI) assistance. Specifically, IOM is conducting a needs assessment, providing emergency shelters and NFIs, and conducting awareness raising on protection mainstreaming.</narrative>
  </description>
